Z||000015||Brandon86SE||12-15-2001||11:03 PM||||I think that car would look AMAZING with some paint!  My first impression was that it was a Tiburon wing as well, but I can't say I've seen a Mitsu.  They don't sell 'em in Canada.  Personally though, I think it looks amazing!  Wouldn't look good on a notchback, but one of the best I've seen on a fastback.  I've always loved the Tiburon wing, and like the older style Tiburon's (before the ugly 4 headlight front).  I would like to know where that is from for sure, 'cause I'll definitely consider it for my upcoming fastback!<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000016||Blacktree||12-16-2001||01:07 AM||||rice, rice baby<BR>dum dum dum dum da-da dum dum<BR>rice, rice baby<BR>dum dum dum dum da-da dum dum<P>sorry, couldn't help it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> Personally, I think a straight wing with the stands underneath (as opposed to on the sides like that one) looks better on a Fiero. But that's just me.<P>BTW, I saw a Fiero around my neck of the woods (Orlando, FL) that had a wing very similar to that one. But all the paint in his car matched.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A><p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||1
