Z||000018||JD86GT350||12-16-2001||01:44 PM||||spent some time sorting through searches, and found this one, still wouldn't mind some more info tho   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>Just because you guys have no imagination doesn't mean you should slam the post...<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Mods/fiero-2.JPG">   <BR>This guy had a little more imaginitive thinking, and came up with something that I think fits the Fiero well.<P>I came across this pic somehow a while ago, and saved it to my hard drive I liked it so much.  It's an aftermarket wing for an eclipse that has been modified to fit the fiero.  If you look at the second link posted above, it's not too far from that design.  I think this wing looks excellent.  For a long time I was thinking of doing this, but eventually decided against it.  I like the look of the stock wing, and it's the perfect width, so I'm using it.  I'm going to make some 12" stantions for it, with some built in adjustment.  At this height it will actually be USEFUL, and yes, I do plan on hitting 120...often as I can get the chance to.  I want to make this car become a weekend warrior (racecar) but still a daily driver.  Some of us like certain styles, some of us have ambitions, some of us think a little differently.  Don't slam that; sure, if you're hanging out with your buddies and they feel the same way, that's fine...but this is a pretty diverse forum, and you never know what may become of things.  &lt;/RANT&gt;<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>from this thread <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011361.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011361.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by JD86GT350 (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Mach10||12-16-2001||04:11 PM||||I don't mind aftermarket wings. I just have a problem with high-profile wings. IMHO they look positively STUPID. <BR>That goes for:<BR>- "adjustable" wings.<BR>- Hyper-extended stock wings<BR>- ANY double-decker wings<BR>- Whale-tails (unless it's a late-80s STOCK Porsche 911  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P><BR>None of these wings could possibly have any positive effect on handling, except by total accident. As a rule, I'm totally against non-functional high-profile COSMETIC modifications. Decals, radical tail-light mods, potato-cannon tips, ANYTHING that doesn't actually make the car <I>do</I> anything different, except slow it down either by additional weight or increased drag.<P>BUT, (and this is a big one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) whatever floats your boat. I don't think you are a retard for putting that crap on your car... I just think your car looks like ass  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> But at least a Fiero has some "Go!" in it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
