Z||000024||88 Fiero||12-16-2001||11:36 PM||||I can see that some of you guys still have a pic of my '88 formula. I converted this car to a GT Fastback and decided to do something different. The wing is a combat wing style for the eclipse. It was cut in 3 pieces and glass to the decklid. setback for doing this is that the decklid was heavy. The center blade was adjustable. The car has a performance cam, a custom ram air and a custom chip that eliminates the fuel cut-off when I hit 6000 RPM's. I also have the Miller Woods Turbo in which I will hook it up once I get my 3.4 block in it. The rims are 17 inch OZ Competition wheels. I already sold those wheels to another friend because I have 18 inchers to replaced it. The car also have a Kid Danger Air Dam, one piece. Interior was very very clean with no rip on the seats or dash.It's 5-speed. It has 73,000 miles on it. I installed the factory sunroof. Unfortunately, when I going thru my divorced I decided to sell the car and a guy who owns a GM Truck Dealer in Oregon came down with a trailer and took my car. I really hate it when I let it go, but I have to straigthen out my priorities and my life first. This was about 2 to 3 years ago. But I still keep on checking prices on the GT's specially a T-Top and 5-speed. I will definately will buy again once I'm ready. And thanks for keeping a pic of my car, it really brings back memories and I look forward in buying my Fiero soon!!!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000025||JD86GT350||12-17-2001||07:45 PM||||yeah!  the definitive answer!<P>Thanks!<P>I guess this post proves everybody's different taste.  I wouldn't want a foot tall wing either, but this one looks really good to me, maybe because its so unique.  <P>hmm, what to do...what to do...||||reg||1
Z||000026||TRiAD||12-17-2001||08:27 PM||||If anyone's ever realy interested, I carry those. This would be a good project for fibersmith (Ferrari_momo) or AusFiero to make a new mold FOR the Fiero. I would supply the wing at COST to anyone wanting to do this. <BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAAAMsSN*Wryq60N*CeWB!hXjfeIaMEc1YxPH9aPzaIXm!17ZpdBFE0Yk*d*dHNFG*GR3SFyLa8KJgh1IKe2Q/xmas-sig.jpg">       <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="red">Merry Christmas!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>Photoshop rendition of planned modifications<BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||1
